I've found there are some occasions where you pretty much HAVE to use auto.  

Because otherwise, you could sit there until the heat death of the universe and not be able to figure out what type you need to get your crap to compile.  Ran into that issue with templating a function where I was trying to determine if a specific value was present within an STL container - the compiler was absolutely freaking out no matter what types I declared, swapped it for auto out of desperation and it ran like a dream.  To this day I don't know what I was supposed to have declared, but it was probably something truly ridiculous and arcane that you need years of experience to get it.

